{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): Morning. Up on the chair for me. Blood pressure is 138 over 82, pulse 76. He won't be a minute, he's with your man next door.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (DOCTOR): Right. What have you got?",
  "[SEG0003] person_3 (PATIENT): Ah sure look, it's nothing. A bit of spinning when I turn in the bed, since last week. Two or three seconds and it's gone. The wife made me come.",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (DOCTOR): Only in the bed?",
  "[SEG0005] person_3 (PATIENT): And looking up. At the press over the cooker. That's the lot. Hardly anything.",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (DOCTOR): Started which day?",
  "[SEG0007] person_3 (PATIENT): Umm. Tuesday. Or the Wednesday, maybe. Last week anyway.",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (DOCTOR): Nausea?",
  "[SEG0009] person_3 (PATIENT): No. No sickness. I'm grand.",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (DOCTOR): Hearing loss?",
  "[SEG0011] person_3 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (DOCTOR): Pain in the ear?",
  "[SEG0013] person_3 (PATIENT): Not a bit.",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (DOCTOR): Of. Headaches?",
  "[SEG0015] person_3 (PATIENT): Mm, I suppose. Sometimes, not really.",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (DOCTOR): Medicines?",
  "[SEG0017] person_3 (PATIENT): Err. Metformine 500 milligrams twice a day, for the sugar. Mizartan 40 mg of a morning, for the pressure. Omprazole 20 mg, the heartburn one.",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (DOCTOR): Diabetes and the blood pressure still going?",
  "[SEG0019] person_3 (PATIENT): Years. They're grand. Not a bother. Parking was a nightmare out there, mind.",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (DOCTOR): Positional test now. Turn your head to the right. Lie back quick when I tell you.",
  "[SEG0021] person_3 (PATIENT): Must we. It'll be over in a second.",
  "[SEG0022] person_2 (DOCTOR): Lie back. Now.",
  "[SEG0023] person_3 (PATIENT): Oh. There, that's it. Only a second, like I said.",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (DOCTOR): Eyes are jumping. Positive on the right.",
  "[SEG0025] person_3 (PATIENT): And it's gone. I told you. Nothing to it.",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (DOCTOR): Crystals loose in the inner ear. Benign positional vertigo, I'd say. I'll teach you the Epley. You do it at home, three times a day, until the spinning stops.",
  "[SEG0027] person_3 (PATIENT): Umm. Three times a day. If I remember, like.",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (DOCTOR): Vomiting?",
  "[SEG0029] person_3 (PATIENT): Well, actually, no vomiting. But I do go queasy when it spins. Nearly got sick yesterday when I rolled over. Just a small bit of nausea. I was making little of it.",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (DOCTOR): If it's still spinning in a fortnight, come back.",
  "[SEG0031] person_3 (PATIENT): Grand so.",
  "[SEG0032] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): Mind the step, the floor's slippy out there."
 ],
